From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Tiberiu Chibici <chibicitiberiu@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 20:04:10 +0200
Subject: Add transport-tycoon-deluxe-music-fm: the Windows CD's FM music with
 its own OpenTTD set

Walnut: the user's Transport Tycoon Deluxe for Windows copy, which has its music only as
fm/9_tt*.fm, the arrangements for FM synthesizer cards, and no gm/gm_tt*.gm (the General MIDI
ones). Both are Standard MIDI files with the same 22 songs in the same order (format 1, 384 ticks
per beat, General MIDI programs, drums on channel 10). transport-tycoon-deluxe-music packages only
the gm files, which OpenTTD's original_windows set (orig_win.obm) lists by MD5, so such a copy had
no original music at all; renaming the files would not pass that MD5 check.

The new package installs the fm files in $assets/openttd/baseset/fm with orig_win_fm.obm, an
OpenTTD base music set (name original_windows_fm, shortname TTFM) made by the new ttd plugin from
the files' checksums: orig_win.obm's song slots and names, without [timingtrim] (the FM theme
starts on its first beat, and Can't Get There From Here has no silence and repeat at its end).
OpenTTD plays them as standard MIDI through its MIDI driver. The plugin's generated_files() says
what it writes, so a caller can check the package's files. The checksums are the user's copy's.

Forwarded: not yet (candidate for Debian)

